<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gol Gumbaz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">completed 1656</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gol Gumbaz is the mausoleum of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-adil-shah">Muhammad Adil Shah</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shahi-dynasty">Bijapur Sultanate</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bijapur">Bijapur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, completed around 1656. Its great hemispherical dome, about 44 metres across, rests on a cube with four domed corner towers and is one of the largest domes of the pre-modern world. A gallery inside the dome carries the slightest whisper across the hall.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gol-gumbaz.jpg" alt="Gol Gumbaz" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukul Banerjee · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gol_Gumbaz_-4,_Bijapur,_Karnataka.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
